      "message": "I\u0027ve looked into the failures on the clients, and *think* everything is okay except for some issues with some chrome pixeltests:\n\n1. The g3 failure appears to be a rebaseline, but it doesn\u0027t use scuba so I can\u0027t actually see the diff, and it will require staging a build flag and updating the expected .gif file.\n2. The flutter failure is because now a blur with kRepeat but no crop rect is correctly being reported as \"affecting transparent black\", which no longer matches the behavior of Flutter\u0027s image filter wrapper, so that will need a flag and updating their logic.\n3. The vast majority of layout tests in chrome are imperceptible diffs. There is a subset blur that has more significant changes, but like the morphology effect previously, I think it\u0027s actually now more correct. The offscreen red and other grid colors are being take into account by the blur whereas previously they were decal\u0027ed at the visible boundary.\n4. The software compositor\u0027s backdrop blur handling appears completely broken. It has a lot of custom code and skia-renderer is fine, so I suspect there is something silly and subtle that is causing the filtering to fail and I\u0027ll need to track it down.\n5. There is a pixeltest that expects kClamp blurring but doesn\u0027t provide a crop (because cc::FilterOperations don\u0027t yet support that). The test explicitly pads the texture out by 50px so I think that\u0027s confusing the \"unbounded\" crop workaround. I can either tweak that workaround, or just do the correct thing right away and have the FilterOperations use a crop to their layer bounds.",
